Z||000000||RFMike||11-30-1999||08:37 PM||||I'm looking at pricing for a remanufactured V6, with a performnance cam and 3.1 crank.  I've looked at several, but I would love to get recommendations from you guys on who you think is best.  Anybody?||||reg||5
Z||000001||RFMike||12-02-1999||11:53 PM||||Nobody?  Anybody?<BR>Has anybody had any experience with Global, Liberty, or Recon?  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||12-03-1999||07:08 AM||||I bought a remanufactured 2.8L long block from Grooms through Ed Parks at the Fiero Factory in Huntsville, AL.  It is basicly a stock rebuild with .040 overbore.  It comes with an 18 month unlimited mileage warranty (consequently I can't make any mods to the block and heads without voiding the warranty). I just got it in and am pleased so far although I've only put a couple of miles on it so far.<P>The only snag I ran into was that several of the intake manifole mounting stud holes had helicoils in them and one was screwed up a bit.  It took a bit of coaxing to get the stud in.<P>I ported the intake manifold and plenums and the exhaust manifolds.  I also had the exhaust manifolds welded on the outside prior to porting.  Using a die grinder it only took about an hour to port both exhaust manifolds.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||RFMike||12-03-1999||07:26 AM||||Carol,<BR>What did you pay for it?  Did it have a stock cam?  What were the shipping charges?<BR>Thanks for the response.<BR>Mike||||reg||1
